course: dictionary
lesson: 8329
title: The many roles of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The word role is a good example. Read the sentence around it to find which meaning fits. «In the school play, Maya got the lead role.» Here a role is a part that an actor plays.
explain: Now read this: «Each chimpanzee took a role in the hunt.» A role can also be a job or position that someone has in a team. The chimps each had a job to do, and the team needed all of them.
explain: Sometimes role means how important something is. «Her kindness played a big role in the team's win.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning, such as "was very important", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A role is a part that an actor plays in a film, play or show.
fact: A role is a job, position or purpose someone or something has, such as the role of a captain.
fact: «Play a big role» means to be very important in a situation.
fact: A role model is someone you look up to, like a big brother or sister.
fact: Context clues help you choose the right meaning of a word with more than one sense.
exercise: «In the school play, Maya got the lead role.» What does role mean here? | *A part an actor plays | A type of cloud | A kind of sweet | A loud noise
exercise: «An older cousin can be a role model, like a big brother or sister.» What is a role model? | A model made of paper | A toy car kit | *Someone you look up to | A cousin who is older by one day
exercise: «Each chimpanzee took a role in the hunt.» What does role mean here? | A type of fruit | A costume to wear | A rope used to climb trees | *A job or position in the team
test: «Her kindness played a big role in the team's win.» What does «played a big role» mean? | It was the biggest play in the school | It was quite a noisy game | *It was very important | It was a dance move
test: «Pretending to be a real person can confuse people, so any role you play must be clearly marked as pretend.» Why must a role be marked as pretend? | So the actor can be more famous | So the costume fits better | *So people do not think it is real | So the play lasts longer
exam: In «In science class, the role of the heart is to pump blood», which meaning of role fits best? | A loud sound | *A job or purpose something has | A part in a film | A way to cook rice
